    "publishedAt": "2026-11-24",
    "summary": "Furthermore, a potential merger between StarHub and M1, coupled with the acquisition of Circles Life, would result in the formation of a new entity with a customer base of over 4.1 million, placing it on a par with Singtel in terms of mobile subscriber share. StarHub will issue around 651.7 million new shares to M1's shareholders, accounting for around 27.4% of StarHub's increased share capital. First, through the proposed transaction, Keppel will deconsolidate M1, including an expected S$324 million ($250.92 million) of net debt, 10-15% of which will be included in the computation of the Company's special dividends when the transaction is completed. The proposed StarHub-M1 merger offers a sense of stability after months of uncertainty, following the collapse of Keppel's S$1.4 billion ($1.08 billion) sale of M1 to Simba in May 2026 – a deal that was halted after the IMDA launched an investigation into Simba's alleged unauthorized use of spectrum .",
