    "publishedAt": "2026-11-17",
    "summary": "However, the company, which had $675 million of cash and cash equivalents at the end of Q3, is making no assurances that it will make the missed interest payment during the grace period. The skipped interest payment and the debt deal enter the picture as Cable One's pending agreement to acquire the rest of Mega Broadband Inc (MBI) it does not already own remains stalled in the courts after CoBank, one of Cable One's lenders, convinced a court to slap the transaction with a temporary restraining order (TRO). NYSE has given Cable One 45 days to submit a plan that shows how it can return to compliance within 18 months. It's a critical time for Cable One, which recently warned that a Chapter 11 filing is a possibility if the company fails to secure a pending financing deal (for about $1.3 billion to help Cable One repay debt tied to the MBI transaction, plus additional runway for Cable One to run the business), and if the company fails to manage some near-term debt.",
