    "summary": "Vodafone is investigating the benefits of different network chips for AI-RAN at a Malaga facility, the company's head of RAN evolution tells an Omdia event. Smartphones & Devices AI & Machine Learning Business Transformation Regulatory & Politics Diversity & Inclusion Leading Lights Awards Omdia Telecoms Research Meet the Light Reading Team AI & Machine Learning Vodafone is investigating the benefits of different network chips for AI-RAN at a Malaga facility, the company's head of RAN evolution tells an Omdia event. First, the heavy AI lifting they do in data centers has left them with a reputation for being power hungry and expensive. Related: Vodafone swells AI-RAN Alliance ranks but skepticism remains The other concern is that making use of GPUs would initially force telcos to invest in new hardware, however pricy.",
