    "publishedAt": "2026-11-16",
    "summary": "The two companies agreed to proactively discuss production and supply plans for core loading equipment to reduce uncertainties that may arise during the procurement process. The 800-volt direct current (VDC) is an emerging high-voltage power distribution architecture that is championed by companies like Nvidia, Google, Microsoft and the Open Compute Project, and is designed for next-generation AIDCs and high-density computing racks. By operating at a higher voltage, the technology reduces the current needed to deliver the same power. An 800 VDC setup eliminates or simplifies many of these intermediate conversion stages, boosting overall energy efficiency Related: South Korea plans massive 18.4GW AI data center buildout by 2035 The partnership between the two companies essentially pairs SKT's data center know-how with Hyosung's heavy power infrastructure capabilities, addressing one of the biggest bottlenecks in scaling AI infrastructure: reliable, high-capacity power supply.",
