    "publishedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "summary": "The device supports up to 576 GB of HBM3E with an aggregate bandwidth of up to 7.2 TB/s, and connects to systems using optical interconnects via the CXL. Hot Chips 2026: d-Matrix stacks AI accelerator directly on custom DRAM for 100 TB/s per card Hot Chips 2026: High Bandwidth Flash promises massive bandwidth and capacity, but its usability is extremely limited AMD shares how it can retain 95% of server performance with just half the DRAM, sidestepping memory shortages with MEXT Nvidia's data center GPUs support PCIe, NVLink, and various memory management mechanisms, but they do not support a general-purpose CXL. However, this would introduce additional latency, which will extend well beyond the advertised sub-350ns figure (which already excludes PCIe/CXL overhead), which could greatly reduce the actual performance benefits provided by extra capacity. These could include custom XPUs equipped with Marvell's Photonic Fabric chiplets, CPUs or other PUs that support CXL.",
    "whyItMatters": "对立讯的意义在于高速互连从服务器内部延伸到光链路，需观察光器件产能、客户认证和连接方案是否改变。",
