    "publishedAt": "2026-11-21",
    "summary": "It is a fully modular PSU, but the interesting bit is that it ships with three 4+4-pin EPS cables, whereas PSU units in this class usually come with two. SilverStone's reasoning is that the extra cable is there for the \"high power demands of Intel NVL-S CPUs,\" referring of course to Intel's upcoming Core Ultra 4000 \"Nova Lake-S\" desktop CPUs. As for the PSU itself, it measures 150 x 86 x 160 mm and reportedly uses Japanese capacitors along with a 135 mm fluid dynamic bearing fan. This \"extra cable\" lines up nicely with leaks from earlier this year, particularly about the 52-core NVL-S variant that has been at the center of rumors for a while.",
